# Copy: no hyphens or dashes

Do not use hyphens (`-`), en dashes (`–`), or em dashes (`—`) in any visitor-facing website copy (HTML text, titles, meta descriptions, placeholders, aria-labels, alt text, button labels, email subject lines shown to users).

Rewrite with periods, commas, colons, or new sentences instead.

**Allowed exceptions (only when truly required):**
- Phone number formatting (e.g. `555-123-4567`)
- URLs, filenames, CSS class names, code, and technical IDs
- Proper nouns / brand names that legally include a hyphen

**Also avoid:** calling Gasworks a “production company” or “production house” in visitor-facing copy. Let that be understood from the work.
